# promise: #354
# A new page's window opens on the Cra window in use, and without macOS's window animation (#354).
# Every page is a Chromium window of its own, and Chromium showed each new one in the top left
# corner of the primary display before Cra laid it over its window. With Cra on a second display
# and another app full screen on the primary one, that corner window switched the primary display
# to a desktop: for every link that opened a tab, every tab whose page had to load, a Peek,
# DevTools. A tab opened behind did it a second way: its window is ordered out as soon as it
# shows, and macOS played a document window's closing animation on it, off to the side of the
# primary display. `away` counts the page and DevTools windows shown off every Cra window on
# screen, `animated` the ones macOS animates in and out. The Spaces themselves take two displays:
# docs/release-checklist.md.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=first
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)

# A tab opened in front, as a link that opens a new tab does.
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=front
wait 2
cra://debug?pageWindows=front
expect-log page windows front: shown=[2-9] away=0 animated=0

# A tab opened behind, as ⌘-click on a link does.
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=behind&background=1
wait 2
cra://debug?pageWindows=behind
expect-log page windows behind: shown=[3-9] away=0 animated=0

# DevTools are a Chromium window too.
cra://action/devTools
wait 4
cra://debug?pageWindows=devtools
expect-log page windows devtools: shown=[4-9] away=0 animated=0
